      "body": "🤖 Posted autonomously by agent acting on the user's behalf.\n\n## Main CI diagnosis: RED 🔴\n\nThe current non-exempt failures are deterministic CPU test failures on the sandboxed `upstream/main` head (`e586a6f2c5f2d1e0626bbe0cb1580d56c12398a2`). The sandbox diff is only the sentinel comment in `python/sglang/version.py`, so these failures are on main rather than caused by sandbox code.\n\n- [`base-a-test-cpu (0)`](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/32727074339/job/97430902140): `test_model_config_reads_resolved_input.py` fails because `test_chain_read_ratchet._returned_field_names()` raises `AssertionError: non-literal key in _minicpm_sala_overrides`.\n- [`base-a-test-cpu (9)`](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/32727074339/job/97430902234): `test_chain_read_ratchet.py` fails with the same assertion.\n- The ratchet was introduced by [`a43592dce5` / #35909](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/35909); it rejects the existing dynamic-key return in `_minicpm_sala_overrides`, originally added by [`092d85eb87` / #30360](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/30360). Two independent CPU shards reproduce the same structural assertion, so this is not classified as a flake and rerunning these jobs is not useful.\n- `PR Test Extra` failures/cancellations are excluded: `run-ci-extra` was intentionally removed.\n\nBase GPU lanes are still running; this comment records the current main regression evidence.",
